THE final blocker for the EasyMesh backhaul link. After 0009 (backhaul SSID)
and ccsp-one-wifi 0007 (STA security suites) got the extender all the way to a
*successful* 802.11 authentication --

    wifi1.3 (phy #17): auth 02:00:00:e1:16:33 -> 02:00:00:d8:b7:19
                       status: 0: Successful

-- the link still never progressed to association, and the connect state
machine just looped auth -> del station -> new station -> auth forever.

Root cause chain, confirmed end to end from the logs:

  1. nl80211_register_mgmt_frames() for a STA-mode VAP iterates stypes_sta[],
     which on this build is { ACTION, BEACON } -- BEACON being added only when
     EASY_MESH_NODE && _PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_, both of which we define.
  2. ACTION (frame type 208) registers fine. BEACON (frame type 128) then
     fails: NL80211_CMD_REGISTER_FRAME returns -EINVAL, because cfg80211 /
     mac80211_hwsim does not permit registering to receive beacon *management*
     frames on a managed (station) interface:

       nl80211_register_mgmt_frames:8984: Mgmt frames have been registered
           for wifi1.3 frame type 208
       nl80211_register_mgmt_frames:8994: Error registering for management
           frames on interface wifi1.3 error: -22 (Invalid argument)

  3. That hits `goto error`, so nl80211_register_mgmt_frames() returns -1 and
     wifi_drv_set_operstate() bails at its "Failed to register for management
     frames" branch -- *before* reaching `interface->vap_configured = true`.
  4. With vap_configured stuck false, the global event dispatcher's final
     catch-all in wifi_hal_nl80211_events.c:

         if (interface != NULL && interface->vap_configured) {
             do_process_drv_event(interface, gnlh->cmd, tb);
         }

     silently drops *every* driver event for wifi1.3 -- including
     NL80211_CMD_AUTHENTICATE. Confirmed: nl80211_authenticate_event()'s entry
     debug print never appears even once, while `iw event` shows the kernel
     emitting the successful auth. So wpa_supplicant's SME never receives
     EVENT_AUTH, never calls sme_send_association(), and the connection attempt
     just times out and retries forever.

Gate the BEACON entry behind !HWSIM_RADIO so STA-mode registration stops at
ACTION (which is all the legacy/non-EasyMesh path ever registered anyway, per
the two commented-out entries just above it). Real BananaPi R4 hardware keeps
beacon registration and is unaffected.

---
diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -8878,7 +8878,7 @@
         /*WLAN_FC_STYPE_AUTH,*/ // Uneeded and requires extra info
         /*WLAN_FC_STYPE_PROBE_REQ,*/ // Unneeded 
         WLAN_FC_STYPE_ACTION,
-#if defined(EASY_MESH_NODE) && defined(_PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_)
+#if defined(EASY_MESH_NODE) && defined(_PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_) && !defined(HWSIM_RADIO)
         WLAN_FC_STYPE_BEACON,
 #endif
     };
